d to pop up a quick video just  to demonstrate something or maybe you  just want to set your alarm in a meeting  or anything like that so there are  definitely some benefits in having this  inbuilt speaker into the active to a  feature that I think is super useful and  super handy for  people like myself who do go traveling  quite a bit to foreign countries and  don't speak every language Under the Sun  is simply the fact that Google Translate  is built into your watch so yes I know  you can use it on your phone but it is a  nice little feature to have when you're  connected to Wi-Fi or the LTE network  now the last feature I want to talk  about here on active too is something  that hasn't been fda-approved yet and it  is implemented in the device but it  isn't active in the device yet and that  is the ECG or the electrocardiogram  basically what this feature does is that  monitors your heart rate and notices if  there are any irregularities in the beat  in the rhythm and that way it can notify  you if you have any heart problems and  you need to go seek medical attention  now I know smartwatches are a thing of  modern beauty but if you're more into  analog watches and you do love the  classic look make sure you take a look  at the first link in the description  below  it's one of my companies called wire  watches which specializes in  architectural II designed timepieces so  if you are clicking on this video and  thinking maybe I don't really want a  smart watch I still love the analog  classic look take a look down and see if  you love anything from the website so  there are some amazing features of  active too but Apple series 5 also has  some incredible features and especially  if you're already connected to Apple  ecosystem this watch is an almost must  have any Apple lover something that  they've implemented in the series 5 and  they haven't had an any model since is  the always-on display usually you'd have  your watch and it would turn on when you  glanced at it or when you touch at it  and then go to a completely black screen  when you're finished however now with  the series 5 you can simply tap the  cover and it will dim the brightness  change the screen and reduce it to 1  Hertz per second refresh rate which  allows a watch to conserve battery  whilst also giving you a 24/7 always on  display now just like the active two  they have come out in two different case  materials the Bluetooth version  loan comes in the ceramic case which is  a light premium quality finish whilst  the LTA model comes with a titanium  chassis now again very similar to the  active to the titanium is a lot more  durable a lot heavier and gives you that  premium feel  which obviously paying for in the price  tag something I really dislike about the  Apple watch is how the menu is actually  coordinated and integrated it kind of  all jumbles around and throws itself  around and it seems very disorganized  the new compass addition to the Apple  watch series 5 isn't that groundbreaking  and probably won't get used by a lot of  people but the implementation of the  compass actually allows you to  understand where you're going on Google  Maps so very similar to Google Maps or  Apple Maps when you open it up on your  smartphone and you see that blue cone of  vision that indicates which direction  you're facing the SmartWatch now also  give you this preview this is super  helpful if you're traveling around and  using Apple maps on your smartphone that  you can find your way around a lot  easier you don't have to guess and judge  walk up 500 meters ago Oh walk the wrong  way have to turn around and start all  over again  so the implementation of the compass app  probably not something everybody's going  to use but the integration with Apple  maps and that kind of vision is  definitely something that is well worth  upgrading now something Apple has  focused on here and something that I  think is actually a very critical piece  of tech in any SmartWatch and something  that would almost convinced me to  purchase an Apple watch over a Samsung  watch is the anytime emergency  international calling so if you're in an  emergency situation you can easily  activate this international emergency  calling and it will automatically call  the local emergency center without  having any LTE plan activated in an  emergency setting this feature could  literally be the difference between life  or death  so what watch should you buy at the end  of the day well in my personal opinion  it really comes down to what smartphone  you have because these watches are  designed  integrate with their parent phone so if  you already own a host of Samsung  devices I would definitely recommend the  active two whereas if you already own a  host of Apple devices I would definitely  definitely recommend the Apple series 5  that's all from me guys thank you so  much for watching if you like the video  make sure you smash that subscribe  button  20-19 style and as always I'll see you  next Monday
 

